                "headline": "Flood Watch issued November 16 at 11:29PM EST until November 20 at 7:00PM EST by NWS Jacksonville FL",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of northeast Florida, including the following\nareas, Coastal Flagler, Inland Flagler, Northeast Coastal St.\nJohns, Northern Inland St. Johns, Southeast Coastal St. Johns,\nSouthern Inland St. Johns and Western St. Johns.\n\n* WHEN...From Tuesday afternoon through Friday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Waves of coastal showers with heavy rainfall at times along\nportions of the Northeast FLorida coast through the end of the\nweek. Rainfall amounts of 4 to 6 inches are likely, with\nlocalized totals up to 7 to 12 inches possible.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
